# DINASTY

Goal-based AI tool discovery site — Express backend + SQLite database.

## What's persisted now

Everything that used to live only in a browser-memory JS array (and reset
on every page refresh) is now stored in a real SQLite database
(`dinasty.db`, created automatically on first run):

- AI performance reviews (star rating + comment, per tool)
- Community projects and their comments
- Hero-banner comments and the like counter
- Quote requests submitted through "Request a quote"

The AI catalog itself (the 46 tools, their descriptions, categories, etc.)
stays as static config in `public/script.js` — it's app data the site
ships with, not something users generate, so it doesn't need a table.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env
```

Open `.env` and, optionally:
- add your `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` to get real answers from the "AI Agent"
  chat button (it runs in a demo mode without one)
- set `ADMIN_KEY` if you want to check submitted quote requests via
  `GET /api/admin/quotes` (send it back as the `x-admin-key` header)

## Run

```bash
npm start
```

Then open **http://localhost:3000** — don't open `index.html` directly as
a file; the frontend talks to the backend over `fetch()`, which needs a
real server to answer it.

`npm run dev` restarts the server automatically on file changes.

## Database

- File: `dinasty.db` next to `db.js` (override with `DB_PATH` in `.env`)
- On first run, a handful of demo reviews/projects/comments are seeded
  automatically so the site looks populated — same content that used to
  be hardcoded in the old version, just persisted now.
- Delete `dinasty.db` (and the `-wal`/`-shm` files next to it) to reset
  everything back to that seed state.
- Schema lives in `db.js` — it's plain SQL run through `better-sqlite3`,
  nothing to migrate or configure separately.

## API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/reviews/:aiKey` | List reviews for one AI |
| POST | `/api/reviews/:aiKey` | Add a review `{author, rating, text}` |
| GET | `/api/projects` | List community projects |
| GET | `/api/projects/:id` | One project + its comments |
| POST | `/api/projects` | Share a project `{title, author, aiKey, description, link}` |
| POST | `/api/projects/:id/comments` | Comment on a project `{author, text}` |
| GET | `/api/hero` | Hero like count + comments |
| POST | `/api/hero/comments` | Add a hero comment `{author, text}` |
| POST | `/api/hero/like` | Adjust the like counter `{liked: true\|false}` |
| POST | `/api/quote` | Submit a quote request |
| GET | `/api/admin/quotes` | List quote requests (needs `x-admin-key` header + `ADMIN_KEY` set) |
| POST | `/api/agent-chat` | AI Agent chat backend |

All endpoints validate their input server-side and return `400` on bad
data — this is the same code path the frontend uses, but it's plain JSON
so you can also hit it directly with curl/Postman.